cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  paper it accompanies.
title: "rPAL-seq: pipeline for glycoRNA sequencing and analysis"
abstract: >-
  Scripts, reference data and an example workflow for rPAL-seq, a method for
  de novo discovery and profiling of sialic acid modified, glycosylated RNAs
  (sialoglycoRNAs). The pipeline covers adapter and UMI trimming, alignment to
  a curated noncoding RNA reference, UMI-aware expectation-maximization
  quantification of multi-mapping reads, differential enrichment analysis, and
  per-base variant signature analysis.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21969177
    description: >-
      Concept DOI for the software. Always resolves to the most recent
      release, so it does not go stale as versions accumulate. Each release
      also has its own version DOI, listed on the Zenodo record, for citing
      one exact snapshot.
